EmuTOS  —  https://emutos.sourceforge.io/  —  GPL v2 or later
Copyright (C) The EmuTOS development team

  NewTOS is a clean-room reimplementation of the Atari TOS API, developed
  against the EmuTOS source as its executable specification. Beyond the API
  behaviour, the following data tables and bitmaps are derived *verbatim*
  from EmuTOS and are therefore covered by the GPL v2+:

    - Keyboard layout tables (US, DE)
        from  bios/keyb_us.h, bios/keyb_de.h
        ->    kernel/src/keymap.rs, keyboards/*.kbd
    - Mouse cursor forms (arrow, I-beam, hourglass, hands, crosses)
        from  aes/mform.rsc
        ->    tos-api/src/vdi/mouse.rs
    - Alert icons (NOTE / QUEST / STOP)
        from  aes/gem.rsc
        ->    tos-api/src/aes/form.rs
    - AES inside-pattern dithers (IP_PATTERNS)
        from  vdi/vdi_fill.c
        ->    tos-api/src/aes/object.rs

  The EmuTOS source itself is NOT redistributed in this repository; it is
  used locally as a reference (see references/README.md).

Circle  —  https://github.com/rsta2/circle  —  GPL v3
Copyright (C) R. Stange and contributors

  Circle is used ONLY as a hardware reference (documentation of register
  sequences) for the Raspberry Pi 4 PCIe root complex and the VL805 xHCI
  controller, which the public BCM2711 datasheet does not cover. The NewTOS
  PCIe / USB bring-up code is an independent implementation informed by
  that hardware description; no Circle source is copied or redistributed.

Raspberry Pi / Broadcom firmware (start4.elf, fixup4.dat, the device tree)
and any SD-card contents are NOT part of this repository and are subject to
their own licences.
